.Dd September 18, 2026
.Dt CONDY 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm condy
.Nd conky launcher and wallpaper rotator
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl dhqv
.Op Fl l Ar file
.Op Fl s Ar file
.Op Fl u Ar file
.Ar command
.Nm
.Op Fl dhqv
.Op Fl l Ar file
.Op Fl s Ar file
.Op Fl u Ar file
.Cm set
.Ar file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility starts
.Xr conky 1
and a background worker that rotates the X11 desktop wallpaper with
.Xr hsetroot 1 .
It changes to the invoking user's home directory before doing any
work, so every relative path below is relative to
.Ev HOME .
.Pp
Window manager detection chooses which conky rc to load.
If
.Xr fvwm 1
or bvwm is already running,
.Nm
uses
.Va CONKY_CONFIG .
Otherwise it waits on the session bus for GNOME or KDE and uses
.Va CONKY_GNOME_CONFIG
or
.Va CONKY_KDE_CONFIG
respectively.
If neither appears before
.Va DBUS_TIMEOUT
seconds,
.Va CONKY_CONFIG
is used.
.Pp
The wallpaper worker picks a random file from
.Va WALLPAPER
.Pq landscape
or
.Va TALLPAPER
.Pq portrait, when the screen is taller than it is wide
and fills the root window.
A new image is chosen every
.Va CONDY_DESKTOP_INTERVAL
seconds
.Pq 600 by default .
Resolution changes re-apply or re-pick as needed.
.Pp
Built-in defaults are enough to run once the sample
.Pa theme
under
.Pa @PREFIX@/share/examples/condy
is copied to
.Pa ~/theme .
Optional overlays, sourced as
.Xr sh 1 ,
may override those settings.
The system file is read first, then the user file.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width "restart"
.It Cm start
Start conky and the wallpaper worker if they are not already running.
.It Cm stop
Stop conky and the wallpaper worker.
.It Cm status
Print whether conky and the wallpaper worker are running, and whether
rotation is paused.
.It Cm restart , Cm load
Stop, then start.
.Cm load
is the form used by the autostart desktop entry, so a leftover worker
from a previous session does not linger.
.It Cm cycle
Walk every file in
.Va WALLPAPER
or
.Va TALLPAPER
at five-second intervals, calling
.Cm set
for each.
.It Cm pause
Freeze wallpaper rotation.
Creates
.Pa ~/.condy.paused
and signals the worker.
.It Cm resume , Cm unpause
Remove
.Pa ~/.condy.paused
and resume rotation.
.It Cm reload
Pick a new random wallpaper.
Sends
.Dv SIGUSR1
to the worker.
.It Cm refresh
Re-apply the current wallpaper.
Sends
.Dv SIGUSR2
to the worker.
.It Cm set Ar file
Pin
.Ar file
as the wallpaper and signal the worker.
.Ar file
must exist, be readable, and not be a directory.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width "-s file"
.It Fl d
Enable debugging to
.Pa ~/.condy.log
.Pq or the path given by Fl l .
May be repeated up to five times for more detail.
.It Fl h
Print a usage statement and exit.
.It Fl l Ar file
Debug log path.
Implies
.Fl d
if debugging is not already enabled.
The default is
.Pa ~/.condy.log .
.It Fl q
Quiet.
Hide informational messages.
.It Fl s Ar file
System configuration file.
The default is
.Pa @PREFIX@/etc/condy.conf .
.It Fl u Ar file
User configuration file.
The default is
.Pa ~/.condy.conf .
.It Fl v
Print the version and exit.
.El
.Sh CONFIGURATION
Overlay files are sourced as
.Xr sh 1 .
Unset or omitted variables keep the built-in default.
Paths for wallpaper directories and conky rcs are relative to
.Ev HOME .
The following names are recognized:
.Bl -tag -width "CONDY_DESKTOP_INTERVAL"
.It Va WALLPAPER
Directory of landscape images.
Default:
.Pa theme/wallpaper .
.It Va TALLPAPER
Directory of portrait images.
Default:
.Pa theme/tallpaper .
.It Va CONKY_CONFIG
Conky rc for fvwm, bvwm, and the fallback case.
Default:
.Pa theme/conky/ident.conkyrc .
.It Va CONKY_GNOME_CONFIG
Conky rc when GNOME is detected.
Default:
.Pa theme/conky/ident-gnome.conkyrc .
.It Va CONKY_KDE_CONFIG
Conky rc when KDE is detected.
Default:
.Pa theme/conky/ident-kde.conkyrc .
.It Va CONDY_DESKTOP_INTERVAL
Seconds between random wallpaper picks.
Default: 600.
Should be evenly divisible by
.Va CONDY_DESKTOP_CHECK .
.It Va CONDY_DESKTOP_CHECK
Seconds between worker wakeups to notice pause, resolution, and
conky death.
Default: 5.
.It Va CONDY_DESKTOP_TIMEOUT
Seconds to wait for conky or the worker to exit during
.Cm stop .
Default: 10.
.It Va DBUS_TIMEOUT
Seconds to wait for GNOME or KDE on the session bus.
Default: 60.
.El
.Pp
A commented template is
.Pa @PREFIX@/share/examples/condy/condy.conf .
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "DISPLAY"
.It Ev DISPLAY
X display.
Defaults to
.Dq :0
if unset.
.It Ev HOME
Working directory for
.Nm
and the base for every relative path it uses.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa @PREFIX@/etc/condy.conf
Optional system overlay.
.It Pa ~/.condy.conf
Optional user overlay.
.It Pa ~/.condy.log
Debug log when
.Fl d
or
.Fl l
is used.
.It Pa ~/.condy.paused
Present while wallpaper rotation is paused.
.It Pa ~/.condy.set_wallpaper
Written by
.Cm set
for the worker to read.
.It Pa ~/theme/wallpaper
Default landscape wallpaper directory.
.It Pa ~/theme/tallpaper
Default portrait wallpaper directory.
.It Pa ~/theme/conky/ident.conkyrc
Default conky rc
.Pq fvwm/bvwm and fallback .
.It Pa @PREFIX@/share/examples/condy
Sample theme, XDG autostart desktop file, and overlay template.
.It Pa ~/.config/autostart/condy.desktop
Typical XDG autostart location.
Copy
.Pa @PREFIX@/share/examples/condy/autostart/condy.desktop
here.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Copy the packaged samples into
.Ev HOME
and start
.Nm .
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mkdir -p "$HOME/theme" "$HOME/.config/autostart"
cp -Rn @PREFIX@/share/examples/condy/theme/* "$HOME/theme/"
cp -n @PREFIX@/share/examples/condy/autostart/condy.desktop \e
	"$HOME/.config/autostart/"
condy load
.Ed
.Pp
The following is an
.Xr fvwm 1
.Pq or bvwm
configuration extract for an existing
.Ic StartFunction ,
used in place of the XDG desktop file:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
AddToFunc StartFunction
+ I Exec exec condy load
.Ed
.Pp
Pin a specific image, then resume rotation later:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
condy set "$HOME/theme/wallpaper/sample-dusk.png"
condy reload
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr conky 1 ,
.Xr fvwm 1 ,
.Xr hsetroot 1 ,
.Xr sh 1
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility appeared in FrauBSD.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Devin Teske Aq Mt dteske@FreeBSD.org
